    <div id="mainContent">
            <p class="Division"><a name="13.18.006"></a>Division 13-18-006<br />Tree Protection Measures</p>


            <p class="digCH">Sections:</p>

            <p class="CiteTOC"><a href="../Flagstaff13/Flagstaff1318006.html#13.18.006.0001">13-18-006-0001</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tree Protection Measures</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="13.18.006.0001"><a name="13.18.006.0001">13-18-006-0001</a> Tree Protection Measures</h3>
            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Construction in rights-of-way, including landscaping, shall be subject to the tree preservation and protection measures of Title 10, Flagstaff Zoning Code, which are herein incorporated including procedures and requirements for root protection, temporary fencing, and grade changes.</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Dirt, rock, construction materials, equipment, and debris should not be stored around existing trees.</p>

            <p class="P1">C.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Trees to be retained should be protected with suitable fencing such as plywood boarding. (Ord. 2017-22, Rep&amp;ReEn, 07/05/2017)</p>

    </div>
